[finding] f-020 Siegel et al. (arXiv:2512.02954) find from joint eROSITA X-ray gas fractions plus SDSS/DESI+ACT kSZ profiles a matter power suppression of 10 +/- 2% at k = 1 h/
**Finding:** Siegel et al. (arXiv:2512.02954) find from joint eROSITA X-ray gas fractions plus SDSS/DESI+ACT kSZ profiles a matter power suppression of 10 +/- 2% at k = 1 h/Mpc, stronger than the fiducial FLAMINGO and BAHAMAS models. HSC-XXL gas fractions prefer 5 +/- 4% at k = 1 h/Mpc.
[tool] tc-261023_1-w1-d-10-51 -> ok: Recorded finding f-020.
[tool] d-10 post_finding {"claim": "Grandis et al. (arXiv:2309.02920) use cluster gas and stellar fractions to infer a suppression of 0.042 (+0.012/-0.014) at k = 1 h/Mpc and 0.184 (+0.
[finding] f-021 Grandis et al. (arXiv:2309.02920) use cluster gas and stellar fractions to infer a suppression of 0.042 (+0.012/-0.014) at k = 1 h/Mpc and 0.184 (+0.026/-0.031)
**Finding:** Grandis et al. (arXiv:2309.02920) use cluster gas and stellar fractions to infer a suppression of 0.042 (+0.012/-0.014) at k = 1 h/Mpc and 0.184 (+0.026/-0.031) at k = 3 h/Mpc. They predict, at 97.5% credibility, that baryons change P(k) by less than 1% for k < 0.37 h/Mpc, and on that basis question whether baryon feedback drives the cosmic-shear vs CMB S8 discrepancy.
