**Finding:** At z=0 the combined extreme HACC point (kappa_w=2, e_w=1.0, M_seed=2.0, v_kin=1.2, eps_kin=1.2, omega_m=0.14, sigma_8=0.8) gives P_hydro/P_grav = 0.99944+/-0.00003 at k=0.101, 0.9868+/-0.0008 at k=0.510, 0.9638+/-0.0020 at k=1.013, 0.9179+/-0.0045 at k=2.002, 0.8698+/-0.0065 at k=3.007 and 0.8400+/-0.0076 at k=3.698 h/Mpc. That is a suppression of 3.6+/-0.2% at k=1 and 13.0+/-0.7% at k=3. Against HSC-XXL (5+/-4% at k=1) the gap is 0.35 sigma, so the point is consistent. Against eROSITA+kSZ (10+/-2% at k=1) it falls short by 3.2 sigma. Against 2309.02920 (4.2% at k=1, 18.4% at k=3) it is 0.6 points low at k=1 (about 3 sigma of emulator error alone) and 5.4 points low at k=3 (about 8 sigma of emulator error alone). This point reaches neither 10% at k=1 nor 18% at k=3.
