[finding] f-027 For the combined extreme HACC point, suppression weakens strongly from z=0 to z=1. At k=1.013 h/Mpc the ratio rises from 0.9638+/-0.0020 at z=0 to 0.9781+/-0.00
**Finding:** For the combined extreme HACC point, suppression weakens strongly from z=0 to z=1. At k=1.013 h/Mpc the ratio rises from 0.9638+/-0.0020 at z=0 to 0.9781+/-0.0018 at z=1, so the suppression drops from 3.6% to 2.2%. At k=3.007 it rises from 0.8698+/-0.0065 to 0.9299+/-0.0055 (13.0% to 7.0%). At k=3.70 it rises from 0.8400+/-0.0076 to 0.9214+/-0.0064 (16.0% to 7.9%). Within k of 3.7 h/Mpc the response therefore grows as z falls, which agrees qualitatively with FLAMINGO (2410.17109). The ratio is still falling at k=3.7 at both redshifts, so the minimum lies beyond the range read here and its shift with redshift could not be measured.
