[direction] d-08 -> closed
**Completed — Find the strongest suppression the HACC emulator can produce at z=0. Then measure how the Pk-ratio evolves from z=0 to z=1 for the fiducial point and the maximum-suppression point..** The direction is mostly done, with three gaps. First, the fiducial z=0 and z=1 values were written to CSV but not read, so the z=0 vs z=1 comparison so far covers only one parameter point. Second, the maxsupp_lowkin and maxsupp_lowM variants were plotted but their values were not read, so it is still untested whether the kinetic parameters or M_seed act non-monotonically. Third, only one of the two planned plots survives. Results: the Pk-ratio emulator is trained at z = 0, 0.1, 0.5, 1.0 and 2.0, and its design bounds are in f-016. At z=0 the combined extreme point (kappa_w=2, e_w=1.0, M_seed=2.0, v_kin=1.2, eps_kin=1.2, omega_m=0.14, sigma_8=0.8) gives P_hydro/P_grav = 0.99944+/-0.00003 at k=0.10, 0.9868+/-0.0008 at k=0.51, 0.9638+/-0.0020 at k=1.01, 0.9179+/-0.0045 at k=2.0, 0.8698+/-0.0065 at k=3.0 and 0.8400+/-0.0076 at k=3.7 h/Mpc. That is a suppression of 3.6+/-0.2% at k=1 and 13.0+/-0.7% at k=3 (f-024). Comparisons: consistent with HSC-XXL (0.35 sigma); short of eROSITA+kSZ by 3.2 sigma; below 2309.02920 by 0.6 points at k=1 and 5.4 points at k=3, counting emulator error only. The extreme point reaches neither 10% at k=1 nor 18% at k=3. It is the strongest suppression found here, but the low-kinetic and low-M_seed variants were not read out, so it is not shown to be the maximum over the whole design range. Redshift trend for the extreme point (f-027): suppression drops from z=0 to z=1, from 3.6% to 2.2% at k=1 and from 13.0% to 7.0% at k=3. This agrees with FLAMINGO's finding that the response grows as z falls. The ratio is still falling at k=3.7 at both redshifts, so the shift of the minimum could not be tested. Files: run dir /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-combo-baryonic-pk/runs/261023_143127/, subdirectories maxsupp_z0, maxsupp_lowkin_z0, maxsupp_lowM_z0, fiducial_z0, fiducial_z1 and maxsupp_z1. Plot: Figure 28 = Pk-ratio_comparison.png, showing z=0 vs z=1 for fiducial and maxsupp. The z=0 variant plot was overwritten because both plot calls write the same filename (dead end x-03). Fix: give each plot its own output_dir subdirectory.
[usage]
[direction] d-10 -> closed
**Completed — Close the remaining literature gaps: the DES Y3 A_mod value (q-07), the depth of the FLAMINGO z=0 minimum (q-08), and cite entries for 2305.09827, 2410.12500, 2512.02954 and 2309.02920..** Two of the three targets are met. The FLAMINGO z=0 minimum depth (q-08) is still open.

q-07 answered (f-025): Preston, Amon and Efstathiou (arXiv:2305.09827, Eq. 3) give A_mod = 0.858 +/- 0.052 for DES Y3 with no scale cuts and a Planck prior on S8 and Omega_m. The verbatim quote is 'Amod = 0.858± 0.052, DES Y3 (no scale cuts)' (tc-...-57). For comparison, KiDS-1000 in Paper I gave A_mod ≈ 0.69 (tc-...-41). The same paper says the suppression must extend to k ~ 0.2 h/Mpc. Without A_mod, DES Y3 S8 sits 0.9 sigma (variant 3) to 1.8 sigma (variant 4) below Planck S8 = 0.828 +/- 0.016.

Other results:
- f-020: Siegel et al. (arXiv:2512.02954) find 10 +/- 2% suppression at k = 1 h/Mpc from eROSITA plus kSZ data, stronger than fiducial FLAMINGO and BAHAMAS. HSC-XXL data give 5 +/- 4%.
- f-021: Grandis et al. (arXiv:2309.02920) find 0.042 (+0.012/-0.014) at k = 1 h/Mpc and 0.184 (+0.026/-0.031) at k = 3 h/Mpc, and less than 1% effect for k < 0.37 h/Mpc at 97.5% credibility.
- f-023: Maraio, Hall and Taylor (arXiv:2410.12500) find that a theoretical-error covariance reduces the Omega_m and S8 bias to acceptable levels for a Euclid-like survey at ell_max = 5000. The part of the text read gives no numerical S8 shift.
- f-022: superseded by f-025.

Citations: four new validated entries were written to /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-combo-baryonic-pk/runs/261023_143127/references.bib: arxiv230509827, arxiv241012500, arxiv251202954, arxiv230902920 (f-028).

Still open: q-08. get_paper_figures found no extractable figures for arXiv:2410.17109 (dead end x-02), so no FLAMINGO minimum depth is sourced to a figure. The follow-up is logged as q-13: read the FLAMINGO full text instead. The angular range of cosmic shear affected by baryons, from 2512.02954 and 2410.12500, was not reached within the budget.
[wave 1] end d-08, d-09, d-10
[phase] critic-wave
[usage]
[usage]
[critique] wave 1 wave: continue
**Critic, wave 1** — continue: 8 findings stand up to the evidence, 5 questioned ('At z=0 the combined extreme HACC point (kappa_w=2, e_w=1.0, M_seed=2.0, v_kin=1.2, eps_kin': The Pk-ratio values agree with the maxsupp CSV (tc-...-45). The Grandis et al. comparison uses only the emulator std (0.002 at k=1, 0.0065 at k=3) and leaves out the published errors (+0.012/-0.014 and +0.026/-0.031). Adding both in quadrature gives about 0.4-0.5 sigma at k=1 and about 1.7 sigma at k=3, not 3 and 8 sigma. The 3.2 sigma shortfall against eROSITA+kSZ rests on the 10+/-2% value, which is not shown verbatim in the f-020 evidence.; 'At k of about 3.7 h/Mpc and z=0, the fiducial point (kappa_w=3, e_w=0.6, v_kin=0.65, eps_k': The strongAGN point changes e_w (0.6 to 1.0) as well as v_kin and eps_kin. The 0.3-0.8 pp difference therefore cannot be credited to kinetic feedback alone. The quoted excerpts show only rows with k<0.12, so the k=1, 3 and 3.7 values are not visible in the evidence.; 'Siegel et al. (arXiv:2512.02954) find from joint eROSITA X-ray gas fractions plus SDSS/DES': The excerpt from tc-...-42 contains only the title, author list and page header. Neither 10+/-2% (eROSITA+kSZ) nor 5+/-4% (HSC-XXL) appears in it. f-024 depends on these numbers.; 'Grandis et al. (arXiv:2309.02920) use cluster gas and stellar fractions to infer a suppres': The excerpt from tc-...-36 ends partway through the abstract. The values 0.042, 0.184 and k<0.37 h/Mpc at 97.5% credibility are not in the quoted text. These numbers are used quantitatively in f-024.).

Issues: The maximum suppression is not established. The maxsupp_lowkin and maxsupp_lowM CSVs exist but were never read. Cosmology was held at omega_m=0.14 and sigma_8=0.8, although the suppression depends on the cosmic baryon fraction. The kappa_w effect is confounded with M_seed: maxsupp (kappa_w=2, M_seed=2.0) and strongAGN (kappa_w=3, M_seed=1.3) differ in both. q-02 and q-10 remain unanswered.; The fGas CSVs were written but never read. The pairing of gas fraction with suppression is the central quantitative test of the AGN-physics explanation the task asks for, and reading the files costs about 3 tool calls.; The z=0 to z=1 trend has been measured for one point only; fiducial_z1 was not read. Two FLAMINGO statements are unsourced while q-08/q-13 stays open: the 'agrees with FLAMINGO' claim, and the statement that FLAMINGO's minimum lies at k~8-10 h/Mpc..
[phase] replan
[usage]
[directions] d-08 [closed] Find the strongest suppression the HACC emulator can produce; d-09 [closed] Resolve the HACC Pk-ratio above k=3.7 h/Mpc (q-06, x-01), gi; d-10 [closed] Close the remaining literature gaps: the DES Y3 A_mod value ; d-11 [open] Read the HACC outputs already written but never read (fGas f; d-12 [open] Verify the contested literature numbers verbatim and close t; d-13 [open] Make the weak-lensing impact quantitative. Extract one numer
**Next steps after wave 1** — All earlier directions are closed and none is carried over. The final wave has about 11 tool calls, so it focuses on finishing work rather than starting new compute. First priority is reading the CSVs already on disk: fGas, lowkin, lowM and fiducial_z1. That answers q-12, much of q-02 and q-10, and the critic's high-severity issues, and it tests the AGN-physics explanation through the f_gas-to-suppression relation. Second is verbatim verification of the contested literature numbers (f-020, f-021), the FLAMINGO minimum (q-08, q-13), and a corrected error budget for f-024. Third, if budget remains, is one quantitative S8 bias from 2410.12500 and a test of HACC's large-scale suppression against the Preston et al. requirement, with the C_ell forecast stated as future work. The critic's one-at-a-time parameter and cosmology scan and the P_grav-definition check (q-09) are deferred because they cannot fit the budget; the report should list them as limitations. The task did not request facility runs, so the local and hosted execution used so far is sufficient.

New lines of investigation: Read the HACC outputs already written but never read (fGas for fiducial, strongAGN and weakAGN; maxsupp_lowkin_z0; maxsupp_lowM_z0; fiducial_z1). Pair f_gas near M500c ~ 1e14 Msun with S(k=1) and S(k=3) to test the van Daalen-type relation, and establish whether the design range can reach the eROSITA+kSZ level.; Verify the contested literature numbers verbatim and close the FLAMINGO gap. Quote 10+/-2% and 5+/-4% from 2512.02954, quote 0.042 and 0.184 at k=1 and 3 from 2309.02920, and quote the FLAMINGO z=0 S(k) at k=1 and the depth and location of its minimum from 2410.17109.; Make the weak-lensing impact quantitative. Extract one numerical S8 (or Omega_m) bias from ignoring baryons, with its survey configuration. Compare HACC maxsupp S(k) at k=0.2-0.5 with the Preston et al. requirement that suppression extend to k~0.2 h/Mpc and with the size of A_mod..
