**Finding:** Corrected deficit significance for the HACC extreme point (f-024), with emulator and published errors combined in quadrature and the published error taken on the side facing the HACC value. Against Grandis et al. (2309.02920): at k=1, (4.2-3.6)/sqrt(0.2^2+1.4^2) = 0.4 sigma; at k=3, (18.4-13.0)/sqrt(0.7^2+3.1^2) = 1.7 sigma. Against eROSITA+kSZ (2512.02954): (10-3.6)/sqrt(0.2^2+2^2) = 3.2 sigma. Against HSC-XXL: 1.4/sqrt(0.2^2+4^2) = 0.35 sigma. This replaces the f-024 statements of about 3 sigma and 8 sigma, which counted emulator error only.
