[finding] f-031 Maraio, Hall and Taylor (arXiv:2410.12500, Table 3) work with an idealised Euclid-like (Stage-IV) cosmic-shear survey at ell_max = 5000 and use Illustris as the
**Finding:** Maraio, Hall and Taylor (arXiv:2410.12500, Table 3) work with an idealised Euclid-like (Stage-IV) cosmic-shear survey at ell_max = 5000 and use Illustris as the ground truth. When the one-parameter HMCode baryon model is fitted without a theory error, Omega_m is biased by 100*Delta Omega_m = -1.317, which is -5.690 sigma. Adding the theoretical-error covariance cuts this to 0.128 (0.249 sigma). With Bahamas as the ground truth the bias is only 0.057 (0.258 sigma). Eagle with the 6-parameter model is still biased with the theory error included: 0.573 (1.459 sigma). In the text, the one-parameter model without theory error gives 'at least a 3 sigma offset in either Omega_m or S8 for all hydro-sims excluding Bahamas'. For Simba, even ell_max = 1000 is biased by more than 2 sigma in all cosmological parameters.
