**Blocked — Verify the contested literature numbers verbatim and close the FLAMINGO gap. Quote 10+/-2% and 5+/-4% from 2512.02954, quote 0.042 and 0.184 at k=1 and 3 from 2309.02920, and quote the FLAMINGO z=0 S(k) at k=1 and the depth and location of its minimum from 2410.17109..** (The tool budget ran out right after the three full-text downloads, before any read_arxiv_chunk call. No verbatim quotes or FLAMINGO S(k) values were extracted. Next step: read the downloaded .txt files (q-14).) Only the error-budget part of this direction is done. No text was read, so f-020 and f-021 are still not confirmed verbatim and no FLAMINGO S(k) value has been quoted. (1) Full texts of 2410.17109 (FLAMINGO), 2512.02954 and 2309.02920 were downloaded to /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-combo-baryonic-pk/runs/261023_143127/ as 2410.17109.txt, 2512.02954.txt and 2309.02920.txt (f-030). (2) The deficit significance for the HACC extreme point was recomputed (f-029). Emulator and published errors were combined in quadrature, using the published error on the side facing the HACC value. Against Grandis et al. the deficit is 0.4 sigma at k=1 h/Mpc (4.2% vs 3.6%) and 1.7 sigma at k=3 h/Mpc (18.4% vs 13.0%). Against eROSITA+kSZ it is 3.2 sigma at k=1, and against HSC-XXL it is 0.35 sigma. This replaces the f-024 values of about 3 and 8 sigma, which used emulator error only. The k=1 result is 0.4 sigma, close to the 0.5 sigma the lead expected. These sigmas still rest on the board values in f-020 and f-021, which have not been checked against the source text. The full-text reading is logged as q-14. f-022 was not formally retired, but f-025 already supersedes it.
[usage]
[direction] d-13 -> blocked (The tool budget ran out before I could read the HACC values at k=0.2-0.3 h/Mpc and the Delta S8 table (Table 4) of 2410.12500.)
**Blocked — Make the weak-lensing impact quantitative. Extract one numerical S8 (or Omega_m) bias from ignoring baryons, with its survey configuration. Compare HACC maxsupp S(k) at k=0.2-0.5 with the Preston et al. requirement that suppression extend to k~0.2 h/Mpc and with the size of A_mod..** (The tool budget ran out before I could read the HACC values at k=0.2-0.3 h/Mpc and the Delta S8 table (Table 4) of 2410.12500.) Only part of this direction got done. I have one numerical cosmology bias from ignoring baryons, but it is an Omega_m bias, not an S8 bias, and I did not read the HACC values at k=0.2-0.3 h/Mpc.

What was established:

1. Omega_m bias from Maraio, Hall and Taylor (arXiv:2410.12500, Table 3), read verbatim (f-031; tc-...-86). Survey configuration: an idealised Euclid-like Stage-IV cosmic-shear survey with ell_max = 5000.
- Illustris as ground truth, analysed with the one-parameter HMCode model and no theory error: 100*Delta Omega_m = -1.317, which is -5.69 sigma.
- The same case with the theoretical-error covariance added: 0.128, or 0.249 sigma.
- Bahamas as ground truth with the one-parameter model: 0.057, or 0.258 sigma.
- Eagle with the six-parameter model and the theory error included: still 0.573, or 1.459 sigma.
- The text says the one-parameter model without theory error gives at least a 3 sigma offset in either Omega_m or S8 for every hydro simulation except Bahamas. For Simba as ground truth, even ell_max = 1000 is biased by more than 2 sigma in all parameters.
- The full text is saved at runs/261023_143127/2410.12500.txt. The Delta S8 values are in Table 4, past character 55000 of that file, and I did not read them.

2. HACC maxsupp z=0 Pk-ratio beyond k=3.7 h/Mpc (f-032; tc-...-83). Values are 0.8284 at k=4.0, 0.7942 at k=5.0, 0.7680 at k=6.0, 0.7479 at k=7.0 and 0.7356 at k=7.84 h/Mpc. This is already deeper than the strongAGN plateau of about 0.789 (f-017).
- Source file: runs/261023_143127/maxsupp_z0/Pk-ratio_z0.0000_prediction.csv.

3. HACC suppression versus the A_mod requirement: this comparison is qualitative only, since the k=0.2-0.3 values are unread.
- From f-024, S(k) goes from 0.9994 at k=0.10 to 0.987 at k=0.51 h/Mpc, so at k~0.2 it is presumably below 1%.
- That is consistent with Grandis et al.'s bound of less than 1% for k < 0.37 h/Mpc.
- It is far weaker than the suppression that A_mod = 0.858+/-0.052 (DES Y3) or about 0.69 (KiDS-1000) would need at k~0.2 h/Mpc.
- On this basis, HACC-level feedback is unlikely to resolve S8. That conclusion rests on interpolation, not on read-out values.

No figures were produced.

Open (q-15): read the maxsupp CSV for k=0.2-0.3 h/Mpc (roughly characters 0-3000), read Table 4 (Delta S8) of 2410.12500, and run a Limber C_ell / S8 Fisher forecast using HACC S(k), which remains future work (q-03, q-11).
