[finding] f-034 Partial answer to q-12. Only two fGas points have S(k) read so far. Fiducial: f_gas(1.26e14) = 0.1214+/-0.0010, with S(k=1) = 0.9779 and S(k=3) = 0.9197. Strong
**Finding:** Partial answer to q-12. Only two fGas points have S(k) read so far. Fiducial: f_gas(1.26e14) = 0.1214+/-0.0010, with S(k=1) = 0.9779 and S(k=3) = 0.9197. StrongAGN: f_gas = 0.1221+/-0.0019, with S(k=1) = 0.9746 and S(k=3) = 0.9121. The two f_gas values agree within errors; strongAGN is nominally higher, yet its suppression is 0.3-0.8 points deeper. Between these two points there is therefore no resolvable van Daalen-type relation, and the nominal trend runs the wrong way. WeakAGN has a much higher f_gas (0.1414), but its S(k) was not read in this direction, so a three-point test is still open. The strongAGN vs fiducial comparison is confounded: e_w changes (0.6 to 1.0) at the same time as v_kin and eps_kin.
