**Finding:** The HACC maxsupp_lowM point at z=0 (kappa_w=2, e_w=1.0, M_seed=0.6, v_kin=1.2, eps_kin=1.2, omega_m=0.14, sigma_8=0.8) suppresses more than the combined maxsupp point (M_seed=2.0). P_hydro/P_grav is 0.9967 at k=0.212, 0.9835+/-0.0011 at k=0.510, 0.9557+/-0.0029 at k=1.013, 0.9026+/-0.0064 at k=2.002, 0.8521+/-0.0094 at k=3.007 and 0.8228+/-0.0109 at k=3.698 h/Mpc. The maxsupp values are 0.9638, 0.8698 and 0.8400 at k=1, 3 and 3.7. The suppression is 4.4+/-0.3% at k=1 and 14.8+/-0.9% at k=3, so maxsupp is not the strongest point, and low M_seed increases the suppression. This is still short of eROSITA+kSZ (10+/-2% at k=1, arXiv:2512.02954) by about 2.8 sigma. It is consistent with HSC-XXL (5+/-4%) and with Grandis et al. at k=1 (4.2%). At k=3 it is 3.6 points below Grandis (18.4%). Among the points read, the HACC design range does not reach the eROSITA+kSZ level at k=1.
