**Critic, wave 2** — continue: 5 findings stand up to the evidence, 3 questioned ('Corrected deficit significance for the HACC extreme point (f-024), with emulator and publi': The arithmetic checks out: 0.6/1.414 = 0.42, 5.4/3.18 = 1.70, 6.4/2.01 = 3.18 and 1.4/4.005 = 0.35. However, every input comes from unverified values. The 2512.02954 and 2309.02920 excerpts are cut off in the abstract or title block and do not contain 10+/-2%, 5+/-4%, 0.042 or 0.184. f-020 and f-021 are themselves contested. The 3.6% emulator value at k=1 is also not in the quoted maxsupp excerpt, which stops at k=0.117. The sigma values cannot be treated as established until q-14 is done.; 'Maraio, Hall and Taylor (arXiv:2410.12500, Table 3) work with an idealised Euclid-like (St': The cited excerpt (tc-...-86, chars 40000-55000) shows only text about the covariance discussion. It does not contain Table 3 or any of the claimed numbers (-1.317, -5.690 sigma, 0.128, 0.057, 0.573, 1.459 sigma), nor the 'at least a 3 sigma offset' quote. The claim is marked high confidence and says the values were read verbatim, but the evidence as posted does not show them. A verbatim excerpt of the table rows is needed.; 'Partial answer to q-12. Only two fGas points have S(k) read so far. Fiducial: f_gas(1.26e1': The f_gas values are supported by the excerpts. The paired S(k=1) and S(k=3) values (0.9779/0.9197 and 0.9746/0.9121) are not in the quoted Pk excerpts, which stop at k of about 0.1, and they reuse f-019, which is contested on the board. The conclusion also rests on two points that agree within errors and differ in e_w, v_kin and eps_kin together. That cannot support any statement about a van Daalen-type relation, including that the trend runs 'the wrong way'.).

Issues: Every literature-comparison significance on the board (f-024, f-029, f-036) depends on f-020 and f-021, and neither has been checked verbatim. The full texts are already on disk, so checking them is cheap. Until it is done, the headline conclusion that HACC falls short of eROSITA+kSZ by about 3 sigma is provisional.; The emulator values for lowM are supported. The comparisons to Siegel et al. and Grandis et al. inherit the contested status of f-020 and f-021. The claim that 'the design range does not reach eROSITA+kSZ' has only been tested at the kappa_w=2, e_w=1 corners with omega_m=0.14 and sigma_8=0.8. The lowM curve is still falling at k=3.7, so its minimum is unresolved. The cosmology axes (omega_m 0.12-0.155, sigma_8 0.7-0.9) were not explored, and they can shift the response through the baryon fraction and halo abundance.; There is a physically interesting signal here that the finding does not develop. Strong kinetic feedback leaves f_gas(<R500c) at 1.26e14 essentially unchanged (0.1214 vs 0.1221), yet it deepens S(k). That suggests the HACC suppression is driven by gas removal beyond R500c, or by other halo masses, rather than by the R500c gas fraction. A controlled single-parameter sweep is needed to test this..
